# Band mass and horizontal separators

Horizontal bands have their usual Euclidean area. Weighted mass then forces
two quarter-mass tiles packed in a half-square to fill it, and forces a
horizontal separator between whole original pieces to lie at an integer
quarter height. These statements allow Jordan boundaries of positive area.
-/
